# Phase 18 P18-V01 — NotWriteDefaultValue writer feature

- Timestamp: 2026-10-16 23:09:36 UTC
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`
- Code commit: `9f7870fe` (`feat(protocol): support default value writer feature`)
- Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 / Fastjson2 2.0.63
- Scope: map `JSONWriter.Feature.NotWriteDefaultValue` across inherited body,
  route, and heartbeat serializers.

## Changes

- Java default-valued bean fields are omitted, including nested DTO fields.
- Map entries are kept as values, so zero queue IDs and offsets are not removed.
- `ConsumeMessageDirectlyResult.autoCommit` retains the pinned Java output for
  both `true` and `false` values.
- Fixture comparisons now exercise this feature alongside the prior eight
  mapped writer features. The remaining 39 of 48 features are unmapped.

## Validation

- An ad hoc JShell probe against the pinned Java class confirmed the
  `NotWriteDefaultValue` outputs for default `ConsumeMessageDirectlyResult`,
  `autoCommit=false`, and `TopicQueueMappingInfo` containing zero map entries.
- `TZ=UTC cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked`:
  passed (122 unit tests, all Protocol integration targets, 42 doctests).
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `TZ=UTC mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed all 37
  scenarios and Java/Rust fixture-drift checks.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.
- Default and all-feature full-workspace tests passed on earlier revision
  `c7c26cc0`; the final full-workspace P18-V02 gate remains due after
  `9f7870fe`.

